g  rights act the standoff in russia we're  not talking about buildback better uh  coming back with a new version we're  talking about this so politically you  could see shannon being that you're in  washington all things politics you could  see politically how the administration  would like to change the conversation  yeah i can see how that would be a good  time for the white house but again what  i'm told is that this this announcement  was very close anyway and that it was a  decision justice breyer had made so it  certainly is beneficial to the white  house and gets us on a whole new  conversation about what happens next  with the court what the white house may  do certainly changes the conversation  that's right uh and politico with their  playbook this morning they say on the  latter point the timing could not be  more opportune the defeat of the voting  rights bill last week was a final straw  for many voters of color disenchanted  with the lack of action on that issue as  well as on police reform recent q poll  showed the president's approval with  black voters down to 57 from 78 a year  ago perhaps that's why the white house  wasted no time in  leaking the information it's presumed  somebody there leaked it but how exactly  now shannon does this work  you know he's still gonna have the job  for almost six months it seems  you know it seems odd that you would  figure out who's going to take his place  until he's closer to the end of his tour  well i mean to me i just thought  politically it would make more sense for  the white house if this was a later  announcement only because then you're  leading into the midterms you have the  summer for people focused on this you  can get out there and campaign as  democrats saying the senate's so  important these kinds of battles are the  reason we need to hold on to the senate  so just from a political sense it seemed  a little bit early to me but they can  start this whole process we've talked  about the names some 